# Milestone: M3
# Covers: t.block() pauses all strands tagged with t; t.unblock() resumes them;
#         new strand started while tag is blocked also stays paused.
# blocked: a chunk-top `,` group cannot share a declaration with its
#          arms.  t.block() / t.unblock() work from script (probed), but
#          the fixture needs a loop under the tag AND an observer that
#          blocks it partway, which means `;` before `,` -- and the parser
#          refuses to mix the two in one group.  Gate semantics are
#          covered in C by tests/rt/test_sched.c (block_holds_a_woken_sleeper,
#          block_and_freeze_are_independent).
#
# Everything below this line predates the re-foundation: it names
# tasks and entry points that no longer exist, and its account of
# what stands in the way has been superseded by the `blocked:` line
# above, which was probed against this branch.  Kept for the
# original urbiscript it carries.
# matrix-row: tag-block
#
# Reason:
#   t.block() and t.unblock() are object methods on a UTag value — M4 prototype-
#   OOP dispatch.  The fixture also uses detach() builtin (M4) and ',' separator
#   for concurrent loop + block observation (M5 chk driver).  At M3 we have
#   urbi_tag_stop() C API but no block()/unblock() urbiscript surface.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M4 with tag block/unblock and detach()):
# # var t = Tag.new()|;
# # t: detach({loop {echo("1"); sleep(1s)}})|; sleep(2.5s);
# # ... t.block(); ... t.unblock(); ...
# # (see legacy/repos/aldebaran-urbi/tests/2.x/tag/block.chk)
